\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Up Club, Big Up Club, Up Talent (recruitment), and Courses are four distinct operating models running simultaneously on ~8 people. Each has different customer types, rhythms, and operational requirements \'97 and Big Up Club in particular demands high-touch, curated experiences (vetted intake, private dinners, premium speaker sourcing) that are resource-intensive relative to the standard community. The risk of spreading too thin is real. A coach might explore: *which product line does the employee feel gets the most attention, and which feels under-resourced?*\cb1 \
